.TH BALLOON 1
.SH NAME
balloon \- the Commodore 64 balloon sprite
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B temple/balloon
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Balloon
is a port of the TempleOS
.B Demo/Graphics/Balloon.HC
demonstration.
It runs under
.IR wm (1).
.PP
Twenty rows of three bytes: the balloon sprite from a Commodore 64, at
its original twenty-four by twenty-one, one bit to the pixel, falling
fifty rows down a cleared screen.
.PP
Everything else in the original is the VGA \- interrupts off, the plane
mask set so a write lands in the red, green and intensity planes at once,
and the sprite poked into the framebuffer a byte at a time.  There is no
framebuffer to poke here, so the port draws the same bits as pixels: the
data, the shape, the yellow and the fall are the original's, but the
mechanism it is really showing off is not reproducible outside a VGA.
.PP
The controls are:
.TF "any key"
.TP
.B "any key"
Exit
.PD
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/temple/balloon.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR temple (1),
.IR wm (1)
